00:04:24,640 --> 00:04:29,960
 And once that happens, that's said to be the blood is said to be in the systemic circuit.

79
00:04:29,960 --> 00:04:36,000
 So when blood leaves the left side of the heart, it's in systemic circuit.

80
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:40,440
 The heart has two receiving chambers, the right atrium and the left atrium.

81
00:04:40,440 --> 00:04:45,120
 The right atrium receives blood from the systemic circuit and the left atrium receives blood

82
00:04:45,120 --> 00:04:47,200
 from the pulmonary circuit.

83
00:04:47,200 --> 00:04:52,280
 In other words, the right atrium is getting blood back from all over our body and the

